            "id": 10,
            "last_updated": "2026-10-14",
            "snippet": "22 August, 2025\n# Congratulations to our IGCSE Class of 2025 on their outstanding results\nBIS HCMC students achieve remarkable IGCSE results with 69% of Grades at A* and A\n##### FIND OUT WHAT MAKES OUR SCHOOL SPECIAL\nOur Year 12 students, having recently started their IBDP, gathered in The Founders Auditorium earlier this week, for one of the most anticipated moments of their school journey so far: receiving their long awaited IGCSE (International General Certificate of Secondary Education) results.\n...\nThis year’s results are nothing short of remarkable; among 128 students, an incredible 69% of grades were awarded A*– A and 97% at A – C*.\nWhat’s more impressive, 39 students (almost one third of our cohort) achieved A* or A in every subject they took, with 8 of those students achieving perfect A*s across the board.\n58 students achieved A*/A in over 8 subjects.\n...\nCongratulations to everyone!”\n**Our 2025 IGCSE Results at a Glance**\n- 128 students\n- 69% of grades awarded at A*–A\n- 97% of grades awarded at A*–C\n- 8 students achieved A* in all of their subjects\n- 39 students achieved A*–A in all of their subjects\n- 97% of students achieved 5+ A*–C grades\n- 43% of students achieved 8+ A*–A grades\n...\nWe are incredibly proud of our advanced Year 10 Maths students who achieved an exceptional 100% A*–A.\nIn addition, 100% of our 11 students in Year 9 who sat Mandarin as a foreign language achieved all A* grades — an extraordinary accomplishment at just 14 years old.\n...\n## Related news\nThis year's group of 153 students completed an extraordinary 1,410 exam entries.",
