            "last_updated": "2026-06-03",
            "snippet": "|Year 11 students Dakyung and Ayoung from BIS Hanoi are celebrating their “Top in the World” results in IGCSE Mathematics, awarded by Cambridge International Education|\nBritish International School Hanoi is celebrating the remarkable achievements of two Year 11 students, Dakyung and Ayoung, who have been awarded Top in the World for IGCSE Mathematics by the Cambridge Learner Awards.\nThis significant accomplishment places both students among the highest-performing Cambridge learners globally and reflects their dedication, as well as the strong academic support provided by BIS Hanoi.\n...\nReflecting on her preparation, Dakyung described her study strategy for exam preparation:\n\"Right before the exam, I completed one last past paper and scored 100 per cent for the first time.\n...\nStudents at the school consistently perform above UK averages across subjects.\nIn the 2025 IGCSE examinations, 46 per cent of grades awarded were A* or A, compared to 23 per cent in England.\nAdditionally, 85 per cent of grades awarded were A–C, compared to 55 per cent in England.\nNotably, 6 students achieved a perfect set of A* and A grades.",
