            "text": "## Strong IGCSE options in Hanoi\n\nBased on the latest published **2025 results** in the sources available here, these three schools stand out:\n\n| School | 2025 IGCSE results | Why consider it |\n|---|---|---|\n| **British International School Hanoi (BIS Hanoi)** | **46% A*/A**; **85% A–C**; six students achieved all A*/A grades | Strong top-grade results, and the school says these were well above the England averages it cited. [Results](https://www.nordangliaeducation.com/bis-hanoi/news/2025/8/22/bis-hanoi-celebrates-outstanding-igcse-results-2025) |\n| **The International School @ ParkCity Hanoi (ISPH)** | **48% A*/A**; **100% pass rate**; 70% A*–B | Strongest headline A*/A share among these schools, with a perfect pass rate reported by the school. [Results](https://isph.edu.vn/isph-igcse-achievement-2025/) |\n| **British Vietnamese International School Hanoi (BVIS Hanoi)** | **45% A*/A**; **68% A*–B**; **100% pass rate** | A strong all-round result, with 256 exam entries at A*/A and 384 at A*–B. [Results](https://www.nordangliaeducation.com/bvis-hanoi/news/2025/08/blogs-and-news/record-breaking-igcse-2025-results-at-bvis-hanoi) |\n\n**Quick take:** ISPH leads on reported A*/A percentage and pass rate; BIS Hanoi also reports a high A*/A share; BVIS Hanoi combines strong grades with a 100% pass rate. These figures are school-reported and aren’t perfectly comparable: cohort sizes, subjects, and how results are counted can differ. Ask each school for its full subject-by-subject breakdown and cohort size.\n\nWhen comparing, also check the available IGCSE subjects, teaching support, class sizes, and the pathway after Year 11—such as A Levels, the IB Diploma, or a school diploma.",
